    "interpretation": "Docs: \"decimals() returns the token’s decimal precision — the number of places used to interpret its integer-denominated amounts. The Token Registry lists WPROS on Pacific Mainnet at 0x52c48d4213107b20bc583832b0d951fb9ca8f0b0, but doesn’t specify its decimals value. The token interaction examples show decimals() returning uint8; see Write Your First Token.\" The chain returned 18, so 1 whole token is 10^18 base units, and an amount shown with 18 decimal places is the base-unit integer divided by that."
